17:/**
18: * The paste box: lines of name,amount,date,note each add a claim, in order, for the named person on
19: * the sheet, and open it for the signed-in user exactly as the open button would. A line whose person,
20: * date and note match one of that person's claims updates it instead: a DRAFT is edited to the line's
21: * amount (when that changes it) and opened; a claim in any other status is an error for the paste. The date may be blank (the sheet's entry date while set, else its today) and the note, which may hold commas,
22: * may be absent. A note ending in " #<reference>" gives the claim that external reference, which is not
23: * part of the note. Every line is held to the claim form's and the open button's rules; it is one change,
24: * so when any line is refused nothing is added, edited or opened and nothing is recorded.
25: */
29:    /** The claim form's amount: up to two decimals (a paste names no claim it corrects). */
32:    /** The longest note the claim form takes. */
35:    /** The longest reference the claim form takes. */
38:    /** The most lines one paste takes. */
41:    /** A line read from the paste, checked against the form's rules. */
57:    /**
58:     * Add and open a claim per line of the text, in order, or edit and open the DRAFT the line matches;
59:     * the claims that went through, one per line. Refused as a whole when any line is refused.
60:     */
